  "prefLabel": "Gen 406.11 Participation in the Work of Professional Boards, Committees, and Agencies",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Gen 406.11 Participation in the Work of Professional Boards, Committees, and Agencies.\n\n(a) The licensee shall receive continuing professional education credit for participation in the work of a board or committee of a professional genetic counseling organization or government agency related to the practice of genetic counseling.\n\n(b) The licensee shall receive one hour of continuing professional education credit for each board, committee, or agency served. The work on each board, committee, or agency served shall exceed 24 hours in duration. A maximum of 4 hours per renewal cycle shall be credited.\n\n(c) Documentation of participation in the work of a professional board, committee, or agency shall be a photocopy of a letter complying with the following:\n\n(1) The letter shall name the authority appointing the licensee to the board, committee, or agency;\n\n(2) The letter shall name the board, committee, or agency served by the licensee; and\n\n(3) The letter shall state:\n\na. The appointment of the licensee to the board, committee, or agency; or\n\nb. The fact of the licensee’s participation and the beginning and ending dates of the licensee’s service.\n\nSource. #10687, eff 10-7-14; ss by #13556, eff 4-11-23 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Gen 400); ss by #14338, eff 10-7-25, EXPIRES: 10-7-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gen400.html"
